!.sandbox/README.md

# Chronos scheduling its own repository writes this developer's plans,
# transcripts, logs and schedule here. `.chronos/.gitignore` holds a `*` too,
# but that file is written by the extension at runtime — if it is ever missing
# on a fresh clone, this line is what stops the private work being committed.
.chronos/

# Local agent tooling: slash commands and settings for whoever is driving the
# editor. Not part of the extension, and it names one person's setup.
.claude/

# Unredacted manager and Tasks captures. They show a real working-directory
# path and a real seven-day spend figure. The blurred copies published on the
# landing page live in `site/img/`.
media/screenshots.png
media/screenshots-2.png

# Plans stay on disk and never go to GitHub. Three places they land:
# `.chronos/plans` (covered above), `docs/` — which holds nothing but the design
# plans and the prompt text the scheduler runs — and wherever
# `chronos.libraryPath` is pointed, so any `plans/` folder at any depth counts.
# This is deliberately whole-folder rather than a list of filenames, so a plan
# written tomorrow is ignored without anyone remembering to add it.
docs/
plans/
